#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a1ed3b7-02bb-5f9d-9c31-7eddaa80fb8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2+3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288545}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288545} :answer-field/id #uuid "35127a82-230c-5025-ac87-eb4dafe53c72" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2292b4c-0ec4-5867-a7de-bf2a67a209e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289115}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289115} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cd8b28a-ec40-5b78-9910-db2d429ee40b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289969} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee2a1d96-a32c-5a2f-8cd6-6537695d26a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289601}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289601} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8e6d5ec-636b-572a-8af3-3a4e8d1a2fd5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a9a10a92-511c-5609-8370-301fff1b284f" :question/math-academy-id "q-236389" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(-2,3,1).$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-system\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"System of equations\">\n<table aria-label=\"Equation rows\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td><td>$=$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td><td>$=$</td><td>$4-t$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$z$</td><td>$=$</td><td>{{field-3}}</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"question-equation\">$t\\in [0,$ {{field-2}} $]$</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3t \\\\ -t \\\\ 3t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-3t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1-3t \\\\ y &=4-t \\\\ z &=-2+3t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124847 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7824f178-edb8-50b7-af7f-1c20209da71b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288859}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288859} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7de61a6-0173-5804-b964-ab226d5ed144" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290104} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df8d42ea-9e9c-5df8-83f1-01576487bff8" :answer/type {