\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-5+t \\\\ y &=7-8t \\\\ z &=1+5t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51453446-4eac-53d1-886a-97ade44372a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5+2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288596}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288596} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ad89bd4-b08a-5a72-835d-1c90077d0a8f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57e6c9d0-0a21-58aa-a326-e7d97383f8a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288643}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288643} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c68e26c-2a49-5627-a8bb-4b00955f9423" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289832} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338c29c7-6dd8-5584-b7d9-c226ef8fb4b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288369}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288369} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b910820-4a10-5203-9e55-4367cfc30c20" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5b1acf6e-f29c-5db3-8b9e-c15a932f812b" :question/math-academy-id "q-236980" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on 