 the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4-10t \\\\ y &=-1+6t \\\\ z &=7-7t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290483 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0d37c05-2222-5148-9aec-f93cfef96b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2+8t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289105}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289105} :answer-field/id #uuid "3edaf7a3-5c39-5fa1-b351-32d25769c0fd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72e40c90-b0e3-54bc-9132-cdc3a3ae116d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288832}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288832} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6dcef5-21d8-5104-bb44-42638c6a463d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d2d5d8fc-9cc6-565a-9a90-d1ac2885d17a" :question/math-academy-id "q-236988" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(6,2,1)$ and $Q(4,10,2).$\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<div class=\"matrix-system\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"System of equations\">\n<table aria-label=\"Equation rows\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$x$</td><td>$=$</td><td>$6-2t$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$y$</td><td>$=$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$z$</td><td>$=$</td><td>$1+t$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"question-equation\">$t\\in [0,$ {{field-1}} $]$</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2t \\\\ 8t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6-2t \\\\ 2+8t \\\\ 1+t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=6-2t \\\\ y &=2+8t \\\\ z &=1+t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9027c748-db54-5587-99c2-c1058d6c802b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288997}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288997} :answer-field/id #uuid "95e1ff01-7f86-5ec2-aa76-45dccb8e20c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290067} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7253a68-2e0e-5a4a-b7ef-ce65062e2f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289565}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186289565} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfc99ef7-3f88-5c2a-903d-32723d02b79d" :answer-field/key "field-2"